- `packages/escher-driver/src/canvas.rs` — the canvas reading and its line diff (grouping, command identity);
  the canvas answer holds no virtual node today (security-plan `decision/virtual-node-crossing`, F20 A) — a grouping
  that names a node's id in it is a crossing change (fork F2).

- Two founder-ratified standing rows say the circles reach no snapshot, tree or graph — a11y-plan
  `decision/circle-drawer-canvas-pixels-only` and layout-templates `decision/circle-drawer-circles-painted-on-canvas`;
  this entry makes both false and re-states them at its wrap.

3. **The circles declared.** `impl Widget for CircleCanvas` gains `virtual_nodes`. Each painted circle, in paint order,
   declares:
   - key `c{id}`;
   - role `VirtualNodeRole::Image`;
   - name `Circle {id}, {d} px`, where `d` is the painted diameter rounded as its label is (`:178`);
   - region: its bounding square, cut to a 700 × 400 content box;
   - `disabled` false.

   The box's size is two named constants beside `CANVAS_BORDER`, equal to `.cd-canvas`'s `width: 700px; height: 400px`
   (`:381-382`). Step 7's check pins them against the canvas summary's `width` and `height`. A square that the cut
   leaves empty declares nothing. No other line of the widget or the app changes. The click stays as it is (F1 A),
   and so do the colours (layout-templates · decision/circle-drawer-canvas-colours-in-code) and the whole-pixel
   label snap (`:80-83`).

- (limits) Each limit is witnessed on the stand:
  - a click on a circle's node adds a circle (F1 A);
  - another circle never covers one (F4 A, CARRY 3);
  - a label's region is the content box (F3 A, CARRY 2);
  - the lint holds no virtual node at 12 and 100 circles (F6 A, CARRY 7);
  - the grouping's index is positional: after an undo and a new click, `c3` reads the index `c2` held (F2 B).

  All in `stand_circle_nodes` e, f, h, i, j.

- Rows (rows files read by search — the union 321,996 B past 250,000; each handle below checked present in its rows
  file or standing list):
  - security-plan · decision/virtual-node-crossing, decision/canvas-content-crossing, decision/coverage-line-no-user-data,
    contract/stable-element-id/stability;
  - architecture · decision/canvas-reading-diffable, decision/canvas-label-region, contract/handler-coverage/canvas;
  - a11y-plan · decision/circle-drawer-canvas-pixels-only;
  - layout-templates · decision/circle-drawer-circles-painted-on-canvas, decision/circle-drawer-canvas-colours-in-code;
  - test-plan · contract/stand-boot/boot-circle-drawer, decision/reserved-graph-id-form,
    decision/mutation-controlled-tests;
  - design-system · decision/canvas-line-form-conventions.

- Graph impact, from the trace `tree-query-2026-11-25-circle-drawer-virtual-nodes.json`:
  - `read_commands` @ `packages/escher-driver/src/canvas.rs:297`;
  - `canvas_lines` @ `packages/escher-driver/src/json/canvas.rs:276` and `:281`;
  - `handler_coverage` @ `packages/escher-driver/src/cli.rs:490`;
  - `virtual_nodes` @ `packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/virtual_node.rs:107` and `dioxus_document.rs:402`.

- Leaned per artifact:
  - the grouping rule «nearest region centre, ties to the first declared», per the fixture replay: 12/12 and 100/100
    own-node, against 69/100 for last-declared and 56/100 for first-declared (scratchpad `grouping.py`, run at P4);
  - the tag at the line's end, per `stand_canvas_commands.rs:180-183` reading a line's first word as its kind;
  - the tag on every canvas answer, so a click's diff removes no layer line.

- Basis for the numbers:
  - the fixture counts (3 spill at 100; 5 under 14 px; 26 centres under a later disc; 109 overlapping pairs) come from
    `circles.py` at P4 (research.md §Sweeps);
  - the grouping counts come from `grouping.py` at P4, both replaying `session_common::circles` for a 700 × 400 box;
  - 17 table rows: `stand_canvas_commands.rs@a5d18f604` `ROWS`;
  - CI wall 2119 s: phase Setup 5a, CI#45636762106.

